From 178898ddefdd345f5641c055f44c3f3ca8356877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:59:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] G1 results: numpy suffices for column filters and
 algebra, not for whole-level-0

Measured under CPython and Pyodide 314.0.7 on synthetic 10^5 / 10^6 sets
and the HiP-CT right-hemisphere tractogram (79,648 streamlines, 39.4 M
vertices at 0.1 mm).  P1, P3 and publish pass by a wide margin under
Pyodide; region tests are borderline on the real data (sphere median
78 ms, p90 146 ms); holding level 0 whole and indexing it fails on memory
(the 10^6 index exhausts the 4 GB wasm heap) and on start-up time.  The
README spells out what that means for the browser engine.

run.py: sets are prepared once as .npy in their own process, so neither
runtime pays for generating them; peak memory is VmHWM (ru_maxrss carries
over from the parent across exec); results merge into earlier ones, and a
failed run records its last error message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
